      array (
        'kind' => 'para',
        'text' => 'Cobb County bills wastewater based on metered water use. That means water from a leak shows up twice: once as water and once as sewer. When a leak sends water into the yard, a crawl space or onto the floor instead of down a drain, that water never entered the sewer. Cobb\'s policy recognizes this: residential customers may qualify for a partial wastewater credit for leaks that didn\'t enter the sewer system, along with a possible partial water credit, once in a rolling 12 months with documented repairs.',
