      15 => 
      array (
        'kind' => 'para',
        'text' => 'A sudden jump in usage with nothing visibly wet often means a hidden leak: under the slab, inside a wall, in the yard service line or a running toilet. Try the meter test: turn off every fixture and watch the meter or its leak indicator. If it keeps moving, water is escaping somewhere. A plumber can locate it, and the repair receipt is what you\'ll need for the credit. See slab leak and hidden leak water damage',
