      array (
        'kind' => 'h2',
        'text' => 'Creek flooding around Acworth',
      ),
      6 => 
      array (
        'kind' => 'para',
        'text' => 'Lake Allatoona isn\'t the only concern. The creeks that feed it can rise fast. In September 2009, U.S. Geological Survey stream gauges on Allatoona, Noonday and Butler Creeks, all tributaries to Allatoona Lake, recorded peak flows far greater than a 500-year flood. The National Weather Service in Peachtree City has issued flood warnings for Allatoona Creek at Stilesboro Road several times since, including warnings in February 2023 and January 2024, and the Cobb County Courier has photographed flooding behind Riverview Landing.',
        'links' => 
        array (
