      10 => 
      array (
        'kind' => 'h2',
        'text' => 'Why high water reaches basements that never flood from the lake',
      ),
      11 => 
      array (
        'kind' => 'para',
        'text' => 'Most basement water during high-lake periods doesn\'t come over the shoreline. It comes up through the ground. When the lake is high and the creeks are full, the water table rises and the soil around your home stays saturated for weeks. That water presses against basement walls, especially the buried uphill side of a walkout, and finds its way through block, cracks and the joint where the wall meets the floor.',
        'links' => 
